ar dealers, credit cards, student loans, a broken system. It's the \"throw rocks at their enemies\" part of the Blair Warren line, and the \"justify their failures\" part too. If the viewer is in debt, the script tells them it's partly because the system is built to trap them.", "This is the enemy: car dealers, credit cards, student loans and a broken system. It's the \"throw rocks at their enemies\" part of the Blair Warren line, and the \"justify their failures\" part too. If the viewer is in debt, the script tells them it's partly because the system is built to trap them."], ["Now, a fair question about this step: most of these viewers have an earning problem, not a spending problem, so why is it here? Because it does a job the other steps can't. It gives the video an enemy, it's the step where Jordan admits a mistake, and it heads off the hypocrite comments. Some sections are there to build trust more than to teach.", "Most of these viewers have an earning problem rather than a spending problem, so it's fair to ask why this step is in the script. It's here because it does a job the other steps can't: it gives the video an enemy, it's where Jordan admits a mistake, and it heads off the hypocrite comments. Some sections are there to build trust more than to teach."], ["My rule for endings: deliver the final payoff, then end fast. That's what this does. There's no \"thanks for watching\" and no long goodbye. The video ends right there.", "My rule for endings is to deliver the final payoff and then end fast, and that's what this does. There's no \"thanks for watching\" and no long goodbye, so the video ends right there."], ["Why call it a \"strategy\" and not a \"5-step framework\"?", "Why call it a \"strategy\" instead of a \"5-step framework\"?"], ["Why \"the top 1%\" and not \"the top 10%\"?", "Why \"the top 1%\" instead of \"the top 10%\"?"], ["Because most viewers are gone by the end. The trick is to give real value first and to make the offer the answer to a problem the video just raised.", "Because most viewers are gone by the end. Give real value first, and make the offer the answer to a problem the video just raised."], ["I sell a $5,000 service, not a $37 course. Where does my pitch go?", "I sell a $5,000 service instead of a $37 course. Where does my pitch go?"], ["Same spot, after your first or second step, but the ask is different. Nobody buys a $5,000 service on impulse, so pitch the next small step: book a call, grab a free resource, or apply. Mention it once in the middle as the answer to a problem, then once more at the end for the people who stayed. The ones who watched all the way through are your warmest leads.", "It goes in the same spot, after your first or second step, but the ask is different. Nobody buys a $5,000 service on impulse, so pitch the next small step: book a call, grab a free resource, or apply. Mention it once in the middle as the answer to a problem, then once more at the end for the people who stayed. The ones who watched all the way through are your warmest leads."], ["It will if you mock them. Jordan's pain state is about \"the average person\", which works for his viewer because nobody thinks they're average. For a business owner, describe the situation, not the person: the empty calendar, the referrals that dried up, the ads that got expensive. Then blame the system, not them.", "It will if you mock them. Jordan's pain state is about \"the average person\", which works for his viewer because nobody thinks they're average. For a business owner, describe the situation they're in, like the empty calendar, the referrals that dried up or the ads that got expensive. Then put the blame on the system."], ["Here's every move in this script, and what it could look like for a sales consultant who helps agencies book more calls:", "This is every move in this script, and what it could look like for a sales consultant who helps agencies book more calls:"], [" Jordan's version: Richer than 99% with 