s? Book a call and we'll map yours out", " Jordan's version: Not sure which skill? Digital Launchpad. A sales consultant's version: Not sure what to say in your follow-ups? Book a call and we'll map yours out"], [" Jordan's version: Car dealers and credit cards · A sales consultant's version: Lead-gen agencies that sell you junk leads", " Jordan's version: Car dealers and credit cards. A sales consultant's version: Lead-gen agencies that sell you junk leads"], [" Jordan's version: It was actually pretty simple · A sales consultant's version: A full calendar was never about luck", " Jordan's version: It was actually pretty simple. A sales consultant's version: A full calendar was never about luck"], ["Two rules when you swap it over. Only use proof that's true and that you can show on screen. And keep the enemy as something outside the viewer, like a bad system or a bad industry habit, never the viewer themselves.", "There are two rules when you swap it over. Only use proof that's true and that you can show on screen, and keep the enemy as something outside the viewer, like a bad system or a bad industry habit, never the viewer themselves."], ["Read the whole thing out loud once. Anywhere you stumble, the sentence is too long. Anywhere you get bored, the viewer will too. Cut it.", "Read the whole thing out loud once. Anywhere you stumble, the sentence is too long, and anywhere you get bored, the viewer will be bored too, so cut it."], ["The Quick Version", "The Short Checklist"], ["☐ Open loops: curiosity keeps going through the whole video, not just the hook.", "☐ Open loops: curiosity keeps going through the whole video, past the hook."], ["☐ Value spread out: the best insights are spread through the video, not all at the start.", "☐ Value spread out: the best insights are spread from start to finish."], ["☐ Specific examples: concrete details, not vague generalisations.", "☐ Specific examples: concrete details throughout."], ["☐ Unique angle: a fresh take, not the same advice everyone else gives.", "☐ Unique angle: a take the viewer hasn't heard from everyone else."], ["☐ One main CTA: not several asks competing with each other.", "☐ One main CTA: a single ask, with nothing competing with it."], ["If it's... → Focus extra on", "(The type of channel or video, and what to focus extra on)"], ["An educational channel → ", "An educational channel: "], ["An entertainment channel → ", "An entertainment channel: "], ["A business or authority channel → ", "A business or authority channel: "], ["A faceless channel → ", "A faceless channel: "], ["A how-to video → ", "A how-to video: "], ["A story or case study → ", "A story or case study: "], ["A list video → ", "A list video: "]], "unbold": ["For your business:", "Try this:", "For your business:", "Try this:", "For your business:", "For your business:", "Try this:"]}, "scott": {"id": "14JHrz6mIf3rHIYbzqLa_GdaU-cp0jq-zLl1NWMcUI1I", "pairs": [["The channel wasn't restricted. The videos just weren't doing the right jobs, and nobody could tell which ones were actually bringing in money.", "His channel was never actually restricted, but the videos weren't doing the right jobs, and nobody could tell which ones were bringing in money."], ["Reach video: a video made to bring new people to your channel. Broad topic, lots of people care about it.", "Reach video: a video made to bring new people to your channel, on a broad topic lots of people care about."], ["Targeted video: a video made for someone who is already close to buying. Fewer people click, but the right ones do.", "Targeted video: a video made for someone who is already close to buying. Fewer people click, but the ones who do are the right ones."], ["Funnel: wherever the video sends people next. A call link, a free guide, an application form.", "Funnel: wherever the video sends people next, like a call link, a free guide or an application form."], ["Now, you might be thinking: \"Bryan, I'm not a trader, and I don't have 35,000 subscribers. Why should I care?\"", "If you're not a trader and you don't have 35,000 subscribers, this still applies to you."], ["Because this isn't really a trading story. It's the story of a business that sells something, using YouTube to get booked calls instead of chasing views. And the part that fixed his channel had nothing to do with how many subscribers he had. It was about knowing what each video is for.", "Scott's story is about a business that sells something and uses YouTube to get booked calls. What fixed his channel was knowing what each video is for, and his subscriber count had nothing to do with it."], ["Back in late 2025, Scott's videos were doing well. 14,000 views, 20,000, even 30,000 on a good week.", "Back in late 2025, Scott's videos were doing well, with 14,000 views, 20,000, even 30,000 on a good week."], ["Then it fell off a cliff. Videos that used to get 15,000 views started getting 5,000.", "Then it fell off a cliff, and videos that used to get 15,000 views started getting 5,000."], ["When that happens, almost everyone blames the algorithm. Scott was sure his channel had been restricted. And I get it. It feels like somebody switched something off.", "When that happens, almost everyone blames the algorithm, and Scott was sure his channel had been restricted. I get it, because it feels like somebody switched something off."], ["But I've looked at a lot of channels like this, and the answer is almost never \"YouTube hates you\". It's usually two things:", "I've looked at a lot of channels like this, and it usually comes down to two things:"], ["This sounds boring. It's the most important thing in this whole email.", "It sounds boring, but don't skip it."], ["If you don't track, you end up judging your videos by views. And views will lie to you. A video with 40,000 views can book zero calls, and a video with 3,000 views can book five. If you can't see that, you'll keep making more of the wrong ones.", "If you don't track, you end up judging your videos by views, and views can mislead you. A video with 40,000 views can book zero calls, and a video with 3,000 views can book five. If you can't see that, you'll keep making more of the wrong ones."], ["That's it. After a few weeks, you'll know which videos bring in calls, and which ones just bring in views.", "After a few weeks of that, you'll know which videos bring in calls and which ones only bring in views."], ["We started with targeted videos. Deep, technical videos for someone who already trades and is thinking about getting coaching.", "We started with targeted videos, which are deep, technical videos for someone who already trades and is thinking about getting coaching."], [" Not exactly exciting. But between them, they booked ", " That's not exciting, but between them they booked "], ["37,343 views.", "It got 37,343 views,"], [" His biggest video in over a year, and YouTube told him it was doing 9.7 times better than usual. More importantly, it booked ", " which made it his biggest video in over a year, and YouTube told him it was doing 9.7 times better than usual. It also booked "], ["Notice what we said back in that chat: it got traction mainly with new audiences. That's the whole point of a reach video. And beginner guides tend to have a bigger market, because there are always more beginners than experts.", "In that chat we pointed out that it got traction mainly with new audiences, which is what a reach video is for. Beginner guides also tend to have a bigger market, because there are always more beginners than experts."], ["Now, you might be thinking: \"Bryan, but the targeted videos booked more calls per view.\"", "The targeted videos did book more calls per view."], ["You're right. The 37,000-view video booked roughly one call for every 3,700 views, which is less efficient than the targeted ones. But it brought in way more people in total, and every one of those people is now a viewer who can watch the targeted videos next. You need both. Reach videos fill the pool, and targeted videos turn the pool into calls.", "The 37,000-view video booked roughly one call for every 3,700 views, which is less efficient than the targeted ones. But it brought in way more people in total, and every one of those people is now a viewer who can watch the targeted videos next. So you need both: reach videos bring people in, and targeted videos turn them into calls."], ["Did It Work? Here Are The Numbers", "Every Video We Made And How It Did"], ["about 200 sign-ups in 72 hours.", "about 200 sign-ups in 72 hours"], [" From one video, made at the last minute.", " from one video, made at the last minute."], ["I want to be straight with you, because this part is just as useful as the wins.", "This part is just as useful as the wins."], ["The webinar didn't convert great. Here's how it actually went:", "The webinar didn't convert great, and this is how it went:"], ["The video did its job. 200 people signed up. But only 1 of them paid. That's an offer problem, not a YouTube problem.", "The video did its job and got 200 people to sign up, but only 1 of them paid. That's an offer problem."], [" YouTube can bring you the right people. It can't fix an offer that keeps changing.", " YouTube can bring you the right people, but it can't fix an offer that keeps changing."], ["Scott's market is huge. There are always more beginner traders. If you're a bookkeeper or a B2B consultant, your market is a lot smaller, and that's fine. You just need fewer, better calls.", "Scott's market is huge, because there are always more beginner traders. If you're a bookkeeper or a B2B consultant, your market is a lot smaller, and that's fine, because you need fewer, better calls."], ["Here's what reach and targeted videos could look like in a few different businesses:", "This is what reach and targeted videos could look like in a few different businesses:"], [" One link, at the top of the description and in the pinned comment, and one line at the end of the video telling people to click it.", " That means one link, at the top of the description and in the pinned comment, and one line at the end of the video telling people to click it."], ["At your size, a reach video might get 500 views, not 37,000. That's okay. If that video books one call with a business that can pay you $5,000, it did more for you than a video with 50,000 views and no calls. Judge your videos by calls, not views.", "At your size, a reach video might get 500 views instead of 37,000, and that's okay. If that video books one call with a business that can pay you $5,000, it did more for you than a video with 50,000 views and no calls. Judge your videos by the calls they book."], ["Write 3 reach ideas. Broad topics your whole market cares about. Ask yourself: would someone who has never heard of me click this?", "Write 3 reach ideas on broad topics your whole market cares about. Ask yourself: would someone who has never heard of me click this?"], ["Give every video one next step. One link and one ask. If you give people three options, they pick none.", "Give every video one next step, meaning one link and one ask. If you give people three options, they pick none."], ["Decide how you'll track it before you publish. One link per video, plus the \"Which video sent you here?\" question.", "Decide how you'll track it before you publish: one link per video, plus the \"Which video sent you here?\" question."], ["Commit to 6 videos, posting once a week. Don't judge anything until all 6 are out. Scott's channel didn't turn around on the first upload, it turned around once reach videos joined the mix.", "Commit to 6 videos, posting once a week, and don't judge anything until all 6 are out. Scott's channel turned around once reach videos joined the mix, after the first three targeted ones."], ["Targeted videos should win on calls. Reach videos should win on new viewers. If a reach video brings in new people but books nothing, that's fine, it's doing its job. If a targeted video gets views but books nothing, look at the next step you're giving people, or look at your offer.", "Targeted videos should win on calls, and reach videos should win on new viewers. If a reach video brings in new people but books nothing, that's fine, because it's doing its job. If a targeted video gets views but books nothing, look at the next step you're giving people, or look at your offer."]], "unbold": ["Watch Me LIVE Backtest My Science-Backed Scalping Strategy:", "We Tested 1,000 Trading Strategies, So You Don't Have To:", "10 Years Of Trading Experience In 33 Minutes:", "How To Get Funded SO FAST It Feels Illegal:", "Liquidity + Timing = The Perfect Entry (You're Missing This):", "I Finally Revealed My Most Effective Scalping Strategy (For Free):", "If I Started Trading Again In 2026, This Is Exactly What I'd Do:", "The ONLY Trading Indicator You Need:", "If You Understand Math, You Understand Trading:", "Sales consulting:", "A marketing agency:", "Bookkeeping or accounting:", "Business coaching:", "Software (SaaS):", "1:", "2:", "3:", "4:", "5:", "6:"]}, "thumbnails": {"id": "1gz4VoJxQW9mt_qVE0l27R_-AwdxTiEZDQ7w_4YUsf3A", "pairs": [["I'll be honest with you. I'm personally not a huge thumbnail expert. I'm a script guy. But this one client changed how I think about thumbnails, so I had to write it down.", "I'm a script guy more than a thumbnail expert, but this one client changed how I think about thumbnails, so I had to write it down."], ["The words on the thumbnail didn't do that. Better design didn't either. What did it was people seeing the same package every single time, until they started to recognise him in their feed.", "That came from people seeing the same package every single time, until they started to recognise him in their feed."], ["Here are a few of the people we've worked with:", "Some of the people we've worked with:"], ["RP Profits is one of those clients too. Here's the full story.", "RP Profits is one of those clients too, and 