hs apart. The only thing we changed was the chart. Here are the six parts, and we don't break the rules:", "These two thumbnails went out five months apart, and the only thing we changed was the chart. These are the six parts, and we don't break the rules:"], ["The title makes the promise and the thumbnail gives the feeling. Here's the same idea from a cooking channel:", "The title makes the promise and the thumbnail gives the feeling. This is the same idea from a cooking channel:"], ["The coloured box gives the eye one place to land. When everything is shouting, nothing gets read.", "The coloured box gives the eye one place to land, because if everything on the thumbnail is shouting, nobody reads any of it."], ["If you only remember one rule from this section, make it this one: keep it to three things. RP's thumbnail has a face, a chart and one line of text. That's it. Anything else just makes it harder to read on a phone.", "If you only remember one rule from this section, make it this one: keep it to three things. RP's thumbnail has a face, a chart and one line of text, and anything else just makes it harder to read on a phone."], ["As I like to say, creating thumbnails is not an art. ", "As I like to say, creating thumbnails is "], ["It's engineering.", "engineering."], ["Did It Work? Here Are The Numbers", "The Numbers Since We Switched To The Formula"], ["\"9:30 AM EVERYDAY.\" A chart, a red arrow and a green box. ", "The thumbnail above says \"9:30 AM EVERYDAY.\" and has a chart, a red arrow and a green box. It got "], ["So it's not the words. And this is the thing most people get wrong about thumbnails. Everyone goes hunting for the perfect phrase, but RP already had it. It only got 2,887 views because it was sitting on a bright, colourful thumbnail with a shocked face, fighting every other bright, colourful thumbnail in the feed.", "Most people go hunting for the perfect phrase for their thumbnail, but RP already had it. It only got 2,887 views because it was sitting on a bright, colourful thumbnail with a shocked face, fighting every other bright, colourful thumbnail in the feed."], ["The Formula vs Everything Else", "How The Formula Compares To Everything Else"], ["I went through 64 of his videos and sorted every single one by what is actually on the thumbnail, not by what the title says.", "I went through 64 of his videos and sorted every single one by what is actually on the thumbnail, ignoring the title."], ["Then we made a mistake. We stopped using the formula for four months, and that one's on us. Filming a day in his life is easy. Making a formula thumbnail takes work.", "Then we made a mistake and stopped using the formula for four months, and that one's on us. Filming a day in his life is easy, and making a formula thumbnail takes work."], ["So we posted raw TradingView screenshots, and RP talking to the camera on a beach, in a car and next to a yacht. Real trades, and honestly good content under every one of them.", "So we posted raw TradingView screenshots, and RP talking to the camera on a beach, in a car and next to a yacht. There were real trades and honestly good content under every one of them."], ["30 videos. Average 4,197 views.", "Those 30 videos averaged 4,197 views."], ["YouTube didn't care that the trades were real. People judged the packaging.", "People judged those videos by the packaging, so the real trades underneath didn't get them views."], ["12,356 views.", "It got 12,356 views,"], [" That beat 29 of the 30 videos around it.", " which beat 29 of the 30 videos around it."], ["Same month, same trader, same strategy, same audience, same upload schedule and same offer. The only difference was one thumbnail. Nobody gets to blame the algorithm for that one.", "It was the same month, trader, strategy, audience, upload schedule and offer, and the only difference was one thumbnail, so you can't blame the algorithm for that one."], ["Over a year of the same black rectangle, and it still hasn't stopped working. A lot of people assume that if you repeat the same thumbnail, people get bored of it. In my experience it does the opposite. Viewers don't look at your channel like a portfolio. They see a shape in their feed, and every time they see it again, the next click gets easier.", "It's been over a year of the same black rectangle, and it's still working. A lot of people assume that if you repeat the same thumbnail, people get bored of it. In my experience it does the opposite. Viewers see a shape in their feed, and every time they see it again, the next click gets easier."], ["I want to be straight with you here. We do editing and strategy for RP. We don't run his funnel and we don't own his tracking, so there's ", "We do editing and strategy for RP. We don't run his funnel and we don't own his tracking, so there's "], ["We also never beat his best video. His two biggest videos are 52,727 and 50,458 views. What changed was the floor. The median video went from ", "We also never beat his best video. His two biggest videos are 52,727 and 50,458 views. The floor went up, and the median video went from "], ["If you sell something, the floor is the number that matters, because nobody buys off the one video that went viral. ", "If you sell something, the floor is the number that matters, because people buy "], ["They buy after the fourth one.", "after the fourth video they watch."], ["Good design on its own won't save you. Three of RP's thumbnails were properly designed, made by a professional, and had no chart anywhere in the frame. They averaged ", "Three of RP's thumbnails were properly designed, made by a professional, and had no chart anywhere in the frame. They averaged "], [", not the thing you do.", "."], ["Here's one from outside trading. Instantly.ai sells to business owners, so they put a revenue graph in the thumbnail that looks like a Stripe dashboard. That's the screen every business owner checks.", "Instantly.ai is a good example from outside trading. They sell to business owners, so they put a revenue graph in the thumbnail that looks like a Stripe dashboard, because that's the screen every business owner checks."], ["Here are some starting points:", "A few starting points:"], ["If you sell to... → Their candlestick", "If you sell to these people, this is their candlestick:"], ["Founders and agency owners → ", "Founders and agency owners: "], ["CFOs and finance teams → ", "CFOs and finance teams: "], ["Sales leaders → ", "Sales leaders: "], ["Business owners who are hiring → ", "Business owners who are hiring: "], ["Ecommerce brands → ", "Ecommerce brands: "], ["Use your iPhone in 4K. Take real photos, not screenshots from a video and never a webcam, because video frames are always lower quality. Keep coloured lights off your face, look straight into the lens, and frame from the shoulders up so you can crop in later. Wear the same top every time.", "Use your iPhone in 4K. Take real photos instead of screenshots from a video, and never use a webcam, because video frames are always lower quality. Keep coloured lights off your face, look straight into the lens, and frame from the shoulders up so you can crop in later. Wear the same top every time."], ["Expression → Use it for", "Each expression and when to use it:"], ["Calm (start here) → ", "Calm (start here): "], ["Smiling → ", "Smiling: "], ["Shocked → ", "Shocked: "], ["A result that's genuinely surprising", "A result that really surprised you"], ["Angry → ", "Angry: "], ["Here's a prompt you can copy:", "You can copy this prompt:"], ["A four-panel collage with a beach, a pool, a Rolls and \"my fan\" with an arrow. Not one candle on it. It did about a quarter of what a formula video does.", "It's a four-panel collage with a beach, a pool, a Rolls and \"my fan\" with an arrow, and there isn't one candle on it. It did about a quarter of what a formula video does."], ["The diagnosis took four seconds. It's a thumbnail problem, not a content problem, because the video underneath it is good. That's what a written formula buys you. Channels without one get a bad upload and then spend a week arguing about whether the audience changed.", "The diagnosis took four seconds. The video underneath it is good, so it's a thumbnail problem. A written formula lets you spot that fast. Channels without one get a bad upload and then spend a week arguing about whether the audience changed."], ["But if you screw this up, you can kill a good video's growth. Test the wrong things at the wrong time and you take a video that had momentum and stall it. So here's how we do it for our clients, minus the button-by-button stuff.", "But if you screw this up, you can kill a good video's growth. Test the wrong things at the wrong time and you take a video that had momentum and stall it. So this is how we do it for our clients, minus the button-by-button stuff."], ["The problem is that a thumbnail can get a ton of clicks because it promises something the video doesn't deliver. People click, realise it's not what they expected, and leave. YouTube sees them leave and stops pushing the video. So you win the test and lose the video.", "The problem is that a thumbnail can get a ton of clicks because it promises something the video doesn't deliver. People click, realise it's not what they expected, and leave. YouTube sees them leave and stops pushing the video, so that thumbnail wins the test and hurts the video."], ["(YouTube's own test report splits the result by watch time, not clicks. Same idea.)", "(YouTube's own test report splits the result by watch time, which is the same idea.)"], ["Test big swings, not small tweaks. A different shirt colour isn't worth a test. A different number, a different image of your buyer's world or a different 2 or 3 words is.", "Test big swings, like a different number, a different image of your buyer's world or a different 2 or 3 words. A different shirt colour isn't worth a test."], ["Stay inside your formula. Every version you test should still look like your channel. You're testing the variable parts, not a whole new style.", "Stay inside your formula. Every version you test should still look like your channel, because you're only testing the variable parts."], ["YouTube Studio's built-in Test & Compare is free and lets you test up to 3 thumbnails, but it runs over days, not hours. For hourly testing with more versions, we use thumbnailtest.com. If you're just starting out, the free option is fine.", "YouTube Studio's built-in Test & Compare is free and lets you test up to 3 thumbnails, but it runs over several days. For hourly testing with more versions, we use thumbnailtest.com. If you're just starting out, the free option is fine."], ["(YouTube Studio's built-in test. Free, up to 3 thumbnails.)", "(YouTube Studio's built-in test is free and handles up to 3 thumbnails.)"], ["This is the part most people skip, and it's free views. Your old videos aren't dead. YouTube keeps recommending videos for years, so a better thumbnail can bring an old video back.", "This is the part most people skip, and it's free views. YouTube keeps recommending videos for years, so a better thumbnail can bring an old video back."], ["The channels that get the most out of this don't test once. They check every week. Here's the routine we run for clients:", "The channels that get the most out of this check every week. This is the routine we run for clients:"]], "unbold": ["The formula:", "Everything that is not the formula:", "Background:", "What the buyer looks at:", "The result, marked:", "You, the same every time:", "One line of text:", "One coloured box:"]}, "million": {"id": "1G6gyDiWEyE6oTNBS56qdIFeZ8Fh6ox_41vsOz2TeuN8", "pairs": [["Here are a few of the people we've worked with:", "A few of the people we've worked with:"], ["Now, you might be thinking: \"Bryan, she already had 256,000 subscribers. I have 1,200. Why should I care?\"", "If you only have 1,200 subscribers, her 256,000 might make you think this doesn't apply to you."], ["One of her older videos, from before we worked together. 882,000 views, and she couldn't repeat it.", "One of her older videos, from before we worked together. It got 882,000 views, and she couldn't repeat it."], ["If you're a consultant, you probably lead with tips instead, like \"5 ways to close more deals\" or \"how to get more clients\". Same problem: your competitor could post that exact title tomorrow.", "If you're a consultant, you probably lead with tips instead, like \"5 ways to close more deals\" or \"how to get more clients\". It's the same problem, because your competitor could post that exact title tomorrow."], ["The answer was her age. She became a millionaire at 20. Plenty of people claim to be millionaires. Very few can say they did it at 20.", "The answer was her age: she became a millionaire at 20. Plenty of people claim to be millionaires, but very few can say they did it at 20."], ["What everyone says → What only you can say", "What everyone says, and what only you can say:"], ["\"I help sales teams close more deals\" → ", "\"I help sales teams close more deals\" becomes "], ["\"I'm a financial advisor\" → ", "\"I'm a financial advisor\" becomes "], ["\"I run a marketing agency\" → ", "\"I run a marketing agency\" becomes "], ["The title came from somewhere else. I don't brainstorm ideas, I steal formats.", "The title came from somewhere else. When I need an idea, I steal a format that already works."], ["Leila's two videos on the left. Ours on the right.", "Leila's two videos are on the left, and ours is on the right."], [". One outlier can be luck. Two on the same format is a pattern, and a pattern is what you want to borrow.", ". One outlier can be luck, but two on the same format is a pattern, and that's what you want to borrow."], ["We picked Leila for one more reason, which was her audience. She has a big female audience, and so does Inayah. Same audience means the same psychology, so the same title shape is likely to pull the same people.", "We picked Leila for one more reason, which was her audience. She has a big female audience, and so does Inayah. The same audience means the same psychology, so the same title shape is likely to pull the same people."], ["One rule, though: steal the format, never the video. The title shape was borrowed. Everything inside the video was Inayah's.", "One rule, though: steal the format and leave the video alone. We borrowed the title shape, and everything inside the video was Inayah's."], [" Advantage: Rebuilt 40 sales teams → Title: How I Brainwashed 40 Sales Teams to Love Cold Calling", " Advantage: Rebuilt 40 sales teams · Title: How I Brainwashed 40 Sales Teams to Love Cold Calling"], [" Advantage: Retired early on a teacher's salary → Title: How I Retired at 52 on a Teacher's Salary", " Advantage: Retired early on a teacher's salary · Title: How I Retired at 52 on a Teacher's Salary"], [" Advantage: Got fired, signed old boss → Title: If I Got Fired Tomorrow, This Is How I'd Get 5 Clients", " Advantage: Got fired, signed old boss · Title: If I Got Fired Tomorrow, This Is How I'd Get 5 Clients"], ["The title gets the click. The first 30 seconds decide if they stay. This is the opening of Inayah's video, word for word:", "The title gets the click, and the first 30 seconds decide if they stay. This is the opening of Inayah's video, word for word:"], ["Did It Work? Here Are The Numbers", "How The Video Did"], ["But the result I care about most came later. She sent us two more creators.", "The result I care about most came later, when she sent us two more creators."], [". She sells an Airbnb masterclass and digital products under the video, and a million views in her niche almost certainly brought in buyers, but I don't have the number, so I'm not going to make one up.", ". She sells an Airbnb masterclass and digital products under the video, and a million views in her niche very likely brought in buyers, but I don't have the number, so I'm not going to make one up."], ["Book a Strategy Call →", "Book a Strategy Call"]], "unbold": ["How I Brainwashed Myself to ___:", "How I ___ at [age]:", "If I Had to Start Over, I'd Do This:", "Unique advantage:", "The story:", "Borrowed format:", "Title:", "First line:", "Before and after:", "Turn to the viewer:"]}, "algorithm": {"id": "1uKia2GXBI592Nrk6-4wS_m_49b0uG7ifWi3uqPEW5R8", "pairs": [["I'll be honest with you. I'm not an algorithm nerd. I'm a script guy. But I run a YouTube agency for business owners, so every week I watch what YouTube pushes and what it buries, and I see which videos actually turn into booked calls. This email is everything I know about how it works right now.", "I'm a script guy, and I don't nerd out on the algorithm. But I run a YouTube agency for business owners, so every week I watch what YouTube pushes and what it buries, and I see which videos actually turn into booked calls. This email is everything I know about how it works right now."], ["And if you run a business, the biggest lesson is this one. ", "And if you run a business, the biggest lesson is that "], ["Views barely predict how much money a video makes. Link clicks do.", "link clicks predict how much money a video makes much better than views do."], ["If you only have five minutes, read the section called \"Views Don't Pay You. Clicks Do.\" That's the one that changes how you plan your videos.", "If you only have five minutes, read the section called \"Link Clicks Predict Sales Better Than Views\". That's the one that changes how you plan your videos."], ["Here are a few of the people we've worked with:", "A few of the people we've worked with:"], ["(Eight videos, one hour. Most of them lose.)", "(Eight videos fighting for one hour, and most of them lose.)"], ["When you upload, YouTube doesn't show your video to everyone. It shows it to a small group first, something like 100 people. If they click and watch, it gets shown to 1,000. Then 10,000, and so on up the ladder.