Studio"], ["First, everything is already there. Camera, lights, mic, sometimes a teleprompter and someone to press record. You don't stress about any of it.", "First, everything is already there: camera, lights, mic, and sometimes a teleprompter and someone to press record, so you don't stress about any of it."], ["Gear is the easy part. What actually grows your business on YouTube is what you say once the camera's rolling: the ideas, the scripts, the editing and the thumbnails. That's what we do at Viral Bangers. You show up and record, and we handle the rest.", "After the gear is sorted, what grows your business on YouTube is what you say once the camera's rolling: the ideas, the scripts, the editing and the thumbnails. That's what we do at Viral Bangers. You show up and record, and we handle the rest."]], "unbold": ["Total:", "Camera:", "Light:", "Mic:", "Teleprompter:", "Best for:", "Tripod:", "Light:", "Mic:", "Teleprompter:", "Camera:", "Lens:", "Memory card:", "Power:", "Tripod:", "Main light:", "Smaller option:", "Mic:", "Boom arm:", "Teleprompter:", "Main camera:", "Lens:", "Second camera:", "Key light:", "Softbox:", "Light stand:", "Fill light:", "Mic:", "Audio interface:", "Boom arm:", "Mic cable:", "Teleprompter:"]}, "edit": {"id": "1-qo8fvNmqzGHifdI28FOddSi3QM-QtveNpd82FLQ-BQ", "pairs": [["Open with your best line, not your hello.", "Open with your best line and skip the hello."], ["If you say a number, it goes on screen. If you say a big idea, it gets its own card.", "Every number you say goes on screen, and every big idea gets its own card."], ["Just want the list to send your editor? It's in the section called ", "If you just want the list to send your editor, it's in the section called "], ["Here are a few of the people we've worked with:", "A few of the people we've worked with:"], ["(11 videos. 98,200 subscribers.)", "(11 videos and 98,200 subscribers.)"], ["We edit his long-form videos. His own team runs the strategy, the topics and the packaging, so we're not going to pretend the edit is the reason he grew. What we can show you is exactly what happens to every video between the raw footage and the upload.", "We edit his long-form videos. His own team runs the strategy, the topics and the packaging, so we won't pretend the edit is the reason he grew. This email shows you exactly what happens to every video between the raw footage and the upload."], ["I'll be straight with you. I don't edit my own videos. I don't even know how to use CapCut. My editor makes over 200 cuts per video just to make me sound coherent.", "I don't edit my own videos, and I don't even know how to use CapCut. My editor makes over 200 cuts per video just to make me sound coherent."], ["And that's the point. If you sell a service, every hour you spend dragging clips around a timeline is an hour you're not spending on your offer, your script or your sales calls. Editing is a skill that takes years to get good at, and you don't need to learn it. You need to know what good looks like, so you can check your editor's work.", "If you sell a service, every hour you spend dragging clips around a timeline comes out of the time you'd spend on your offer, your script and your sales calls. Editing takes years to get good at, and you can skip all of that. Just learn what good looks like, so you can check your editor's work."], ["That's what this email is for. It's a checklist you hand to an editor, and a way to check their work in about 15 minutes.", "This email gives you a checklist to hand to an editor, and a way to check their work in about 15 minutes."], ["Chamath doesn't read a script to a camera. He gets interviewed. Someone sits off camera and asks him questions, and he answers in his own words.", "Instead of reading a script to a camera, Chamath gets interviewed. Someone sits off camera and asks him questions, and he answers in his own words."], ["Then the edit removes every question. What's left plays like he's talking straight to you. You get the energy of a real conversation, without the stiff reading-off-a-teleprompter feel.", "Then the edit removes every question, so what's left plays like he's talking straight to you. You get the energy of a real conversation without the stiff feel of someone reading off a teleprompter."], ["(Same moment, two cameras. Every cut switches between them.)", "(The same moment from two cameras. Every cut switches between them.)"], ["Step 1: Cut Everything That Doesn't Earn The Next Line", "Step 1: Cut The Questions, Restarts And Repeats"], ["The first pass is pure cutting. Questions, restarts, ums, the warm-up before a good answer, and any answer he gave twice. Only the better version stays.", "The first pass is all cutting. Out go the questions, the restarts, the ums, the warm-up before a good answer and any answer he gave twice, where only the better version stays."], ["The rule we use is the same one I use on scripts. If the first sentence doesn't get you to the second sentence, it gets cut. For every line, ask: can this go without making the video weaker? If yes, it goes.", "We use the same rule I use on scripts: if the first sentence doesn't get you to the second sentence, it gets cut. For every line, ask whether it can go without making the video weaker. If it can, it goes."], ["Step 2: Tighten It, But Keep It Human", "Step 2: Tighten The Gaps Between Sentences"], ["But not all of it. Cut every single breath and you sound like a robot. The test we use: listen back without watching the screen. If you get bored, it's too slow. If you can't keep up, it's too fast.", "Don't cut all of it, though, because if you cut every single breath you sound like a robot. To test it, listen back without watching the screen. If you get bored, it's too slow, and if you can't keep up, it's too fast."], ["Then the title card hits. Only after that does the video go back to him in the chair.", "Then the title card comes in, and only after that does the video go back to him in the chair."], ["The opening has one job: prove the viewer clicked on the right video. If the title promises 30 years of business advice, the first thing they hear should be some of that advice.", "The opening is there to prove the viewer clicked on the right video. If the title promises 30 years of business advice, the first thing they hear should be some of that advice."], ["Here's the rule that holds people the longest: something on screen changes every 2 or 3 sentences. A switch to the other camera, a text card, a chart, a slow push in. Leave a talking head untouched for 20 seconds and people start scrolling.", "The rule that holds people the longest is that something on screen changes every 2 or 3 sentences. That could be a switch to the other camera, a text card, a chart or a slow push in. Leave a talking head untouched for 20 seconds and people start scrolling."], ["Notice what's missing. No flashing emojis, no spinning zooms, no meme sound effects. Every change is calm and it all looks expensive. Simple graphics that back up the words beat flashy ones that fight them.", "You won't see flashing emojis, spinning zooms or meme sound effects. Every change is calm, and it all looks expensive. Keep the graphics simple and make them back up what's being said."], ["(One idea, one card.)", "(Each big idea gets a card to itself.)"], ["If he says a number, you see the number. When he talks about compound interest, a table builds year by year. When he mentions November 2021, it lands on a chart. When he compares two people, you see two lines.", "If he says a number, you see the number. Compound interest gets a table that builds year by year, November 2021 lands on a chart, and a comparison between two people shows up as two lines."], ["(Numbers are hard to hear and easy to see.)", "(A number is easier to take in when you can see it.)"], ["For a business owner, this is your biggest edge. Your client results, your prices, your before and after numbers, all of it should be on screen. Nobody remembers \"we grew their revenue a lot\". They remember the chart.", "For a business owner, this is your biggest edge. Put your client results, prices and before and after numbers on screen. People remember a chart much longer than a line like \"we grew their revenue a lot\"."], ["On every video we edit, the music comes up during the opening and the chapter cards, then drops right down whenever someone's talking. His voice always wins. Small sound effects, like a soft whoosh, come in when a card or chart appears, so nothing just pops up in silence. Silent pop-ups look cheap.", "On every video we edit, the music comes up during the opening and the chapter cards, then drops right down whenever someone's talking, so his voice is always on top. Small sound effects, like a soft whoosh, come in when a card or chart appears, because a card that pops up in silence looks cheap."], ["(Loud between the words. Quiet under them.)", "(The music is loud between the words and quiet under them.)"], ["Then it's exported at the volume level YouTube expects, so you're not quieter or louder than every other video in someone's feed. Your editor will know this as -14 LUFS. You don't need to know what that means. Just ask for it.", "Then it's exported at the volume level YouTube expects, so you're not quieter or louder than every other video in someone's feed. Your editor will know this as -14 LUFS. You don't need to know what that means, just ask for it."], [" \"Export at YouTube loudness, -14 LUFS. And send it to me once, finished, not in pieces.\"", " \"Export at YouTube loudness, -14 LUFS. And send me the whole finished video in one go.\""], ["☐ Opens on the best lines from the whole recording, not a hello", "☐ Opens on the best lines from the whole recording, with no hello first"], ["A good editor with a bad brief still makes a bad video. Fill this in every time, and always give timestamps. \"The bit about pricing\" means nothing. \"14:32 to 15:10\" does.", "A good editor with a bad brief still makes a bad video. Fill this in every time, and always give timestamps. Write \"14:32 to 15:10\" instead of \"the bit about pricing\"."], ["What to write → Example", "(What to write, with an example)"], ["Title → ", "Title: "], ["The promise in one sentence → ", "The promise in one sentence: "], ["Your 3 best lines for the opening → ", "Your 3 best lines for the opening: "], ["Chapters → ", "Chapters: "], ["Numbers to put on screen → ", "Numbers to put on screen: "], ["One-liners for text cards → ", "One-liners for text cards: "], ["Anything to cut → ", "Anything to cut: "], ["Deadline → ", "Deadline: "], ["You don't need to learn editing. You need an editor, and a way to get them editing in your style fast. Here's how we do it.", "You can skip learning editing. Get an editor, and get them editing in your style fast. This is how we do it."], ["You're not a billionaire with a film crew, and you don't need to be. Everything in this checklist works for a consultant at a desk.", "You don't need to be a billionaire with a film crew. Everything in this checklist works for a consultant at a desk."], ["Your viewers aren't there for flashy editing. They're there to work out if you're the person who can solve their problem. A clean edit just makes sure they stay long enough to decide.", "Your viewers are there to work out if you're the person who can solve their problem. A clean edit keeps them watching long enough to decide."], ["If you'd rather never think about editing again, we'll do it for you. Same team, same checklist, same standard as the videos you just saw.", "If you'd rather never think about editing again, we'll do it for you, with the same team, checklist and standard as the videos you just saw."]], "unbold": ["Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:", "Tell your editor:"]}, "claude": {"id": "1VxLy8Jy2nu7GVoJXXI3lvYyA62j5LmixJq82Dq6FwyA", "pairs": [["Hey, I'm Mauricio, co-founder of Viral Bangers. Editing is my whole world. My team and I have edited over 1,500 long-form YouTube videos, and a few weeks ago I got obsessed with editing using AI.", "Hey, I'm Mauricio, co-founder of Viral Bangers, and editing is my whole world. My team and I have edited over 1,500 long-form YouTube videos, and a few weeks ago I got obsessed with editing using AI."], ["Here's the whole process in one breath:", "The whole process looks like this:"], ["Before you get excited, here's the honest part.", "What you need first:"], [" You need a computer (not a phone), a Claude subscription, and some patience. Your first animation will take an hour or two. By your fifth video it gets fast, because you're reusing templates instead of starting from zero.", " a computer (not a phone), a Claude subscription and some patience. Your first animation will take an hour or two, and by your fifth video it gets fast because you're reusing templates instead of starting from zero."], ["And if you run a business, you don't need Hollywood. You need three or four animations you reuse in every video: a roadmap in the hook, your process, and a before and after number. I'll show you exactly how to get those near the end.", "And if you run a business, three or four animations you reuse in every video are enough: a roadmap in the hook, your process, and a before and after number. I'll show you exactly how to get those near the end."], ["Here are a few of the people we've worked with:", "A few of the people we've worked with:"], ["Everything in this guide is how I actually use AI inside the agency. Nothing is held back.", "Everything in this guide is how I actually use AI inside the agency, and I haven't held anything back."], ["Word → What it means", "Word: what it means"], ["Claude Code → ", "Claude Code: "], ["HyperFrames → ", "HyperFrames: "], ["FFmpeg → ", "FFmpeg: "], ["Node → ", "Node: 