that Claude works like a fast editor who also happens to code. "], ["The tool doesn't make the video good. You do. You're the editor.", "Whether the video turns out good still depends on you, because you're the editor."], ["And I still got AI slop. The same flat, generic stuff you see everywhere.", "And I still got AI slop, the same flat, generic stuff you see everywhere."], ["(Clean, but flat. Nothing has depth and nothing feels alive.)", "(Clean, but flat, with no depth and nothing that feels alive.)"], ["In 15 minutes he gave me three pieces of advice that changed everything. Those three pieces are Steps 1, 2 and 3 below.", "In 15 minutes he gave me three pieces of advice, and they became Steps 1, 2 and 3 below."], [".) The first thing he told me: the newest Claude models are very good at analysing video, frame by frame. So you don't need any extra tools. People will tell you to set up a notebook or a database first. You don't need any of that.", ".) The first thing he told me was that the newest Claude models are very good at analysing video frame by frame, so you don't need any extra tools. People will tell you to set up a notebook or a database first, but you can skip all of that."], ["Think about how you'd brief a real editor. You wouldn't say \"make it nice\". You'd send references and show them what you want. That's exactly what you're doing here.", "This is how you'd brief a real editor too: you send them references and show them what you want."], [" Here's the one I used, cleaned up so you can copy it:", " This is the one I used, cleaned up so you can copy it:"], ["This one takes about an hour and uses a lot of credits. That's normal. Let it run.", "This one takes about an hour and uses a lot of credits, which is normal, so just let it run."], ["Here's what came out of one prompt plus a Nano Banana image. On the left is the real creator. On the right is what my AI analysis produced.", "This is what came out of one prompt plus a Nano Banana image. The real creator is on the left, and what my AI analysis produced is on the right."], [" happens on screen. It doesn't tell Claude ", " happens on screen, but leaves out "], ["A real motion graphic isn't one layer doing one movement. It's a background, a midground and a foreground, and each one has its own life. Everything moves, all the time.", "A real motion graphic has a background, a midground and a foreground, each with its own movement, and something is always moving."], ["So here are the three rules I now give Claude on every animation.", "These are the three rules I now give Claude on every animation."], [" Split the frame into foreground, midground and background. When the camera pushes in, each layer travels at a different speed. The background barely moves, the midground moves a little, and the foreground moves the fastest. If everything moves at the same speed, it's not a camera move. It's a zoom, and it looks cheap.", " Split the frame into foreground, midground and background. When the camera pushes in, each layer travels at a different speed. The background barely moves, the midground moves a little, and the foreground moves the fastest. If everything moves at the same speed, you get a zoom instead of a camera move, and it looks cheap."], [".) Now let's put the steps together. Here's the first animation I wanted to copy, a camera move through layers: clouds, men in suits, a city, cars and stacks of money.", ".) Now to put the steps together. The first animation I wanted to copy was a camera move through layers: clouds, men in suits, a city, cars and stacks of money."], ["Pretty close. With a few more minutes of refining I'd use this in a real video. And the only thing I did differently was treat the AI the way an editor works.", "It's pretty close, and with a few more minutes of refining I'd use this in a real video. The only thing I did differently was treat the AI the way an editor works."], [".) This one looks simple, but it's actually two scenes, not one 